TOUCH(1)                       P32W Unix                        TOUCH(1)

NAME
       touch - set the time of files, creating them

SYNOPSIS
       touch [-c] file ...

DESCRIPTION
       touch sets the modification time of each file that exists to
       now (see utime(2)), leaving its contents alone. A file that
       does not exist is created, empty and with mode 666 less the
       umask.

       Setting the time needs ownership of the file or write
       permission on it (root may always).

OPTIONS
       -c     do not create files that do not exist (and say
              nothing about them).
       -a, -m accepted and ignored: P32W Unix keeps only the
              modification time.
       --     ends the options.

EXAMPLES
       touch /usr/ken/.sh_history
       touch *.c                     make will rebuild everything

EXIT STATUS
       0 if every file was touched; 1 if any could not be (touch
       says why and goes on); 2 for a usage error (no file, an
       unknown option).

SEE ALSO
       ls(1), make(1), utime(2)

BUGS
       There are no -r or -t options: the time is always now.
